<p><code>pop-parser</code> splits a string a person typed into fields. <code>NameParser</code> turns <code>Dr. John Michael Smith Jr.</code>
into a salutation, first, middle and last name and a suffix; <code>AddressParser</code> turns <code>123 Main St Apt 4B, Springfield, IL 62704</code> into street number, name, route type, unit, city, state and postal code. Both are
native — no third-party parsing library.</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
